[0.482, "o", "  Q10 What is the penalty for a data centre fire?    NO   p=0.040   0.483 s\r\n  document sent to a server    0\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "  input tokens billed          0\r\n  one-off prefill                5.893 s\r\n  mean per question              0.447 s\r\n  total for 10 questions         4.475 s\r\n  kernel rust-ffm (native abi 6), 16 worker threads, amd64\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "  timings written to /root/demo/harriet.json\r\n"]
[4.044, "o", "  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n"]
[0.051, "o", "\r\n                              \u001b[1;33m      TypeSafe Jev\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m           Harriet\u001b[0m\r\n  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n  correct of 10               \u001b[1;33m                10\u001b[0m\u001b[0m                 7\u001b[0m\r\n  total, cold start           \u001b[1;33m             2.71s\u001b[0m\u001b[0m            10.36s\u001b[0m\r\n  one-off prefill             \u001b[0m               n/a\u001b[0m\u001b[0m             5.89s\u001b[0m\r\n  marginal per question       \u001b[1;33m            0.271s\u001b[0m\u001b[0m            0.447s\u001b[0m\r\n  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n  document sent to a server   \u001b[0m               10x\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m                 0\u001b[0m\r\n  input tokens billed         \u001b[0m              7292\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m                 0\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  runs offline                \u001b[0m                no\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m               yes\u001b[0m\r\n  prefix physically shared    \u001b[0m               n/a\u001b[0m\u001b[0m              True\u001b[0m\r\n  model                       \u001b[0m        jev-1.13.0\u001b[0m\u001b[0m qwen3.5-4b-q4_k_m\u001b[0m\r\n  kernel                      \u001b[0m            hosted\u001b[0m\u001b[0m          rust-ffm\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  \u001b[1;31mWe lose on both measured axes: three answers and 3.8x on wall clock.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  \u001b[2mDISCLOSURE\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mWe do not know what hardware Jev runs on. Not the device, not how many, not\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mwhether requests were batched. Its timings include the network round trip from\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mthis machine, so they flatter it on network and penalise it on nothing.\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mHarriet's host is stated and it is a CPU: RunPod cpu3c, 32 vCPU AMD EPYC 9655P (Zen 5), 16 worker threads.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  \u001b[2mRead the wall-clock column as two systems on unknown-vs-known hardware, not as\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  \u001b[2ma like-for-like comparison. The columns below the line are the ones that do not\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  \u001b[2mdepend on whose machine is bigger.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2mTen questions about one contract, gold labels written by us. A demo, not a\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mbenchmark -- the measured benchmark position is JevBench, in ../2026-09-21-jevbench-baseline.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.005, "x", "0"]
